{"id": "DehLs3xxHL8", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "Did you know Maa DURGA's name came from a DEMON? 🔱 She earned it with fifteen arrows.\n\nThe demon Durgama pleased Brahma and asked for one boon: ALL the Vedas. The rishis forgot every mantra, the yagnas\nstopped, and no rain fell for a hundred years. The rishis prayed in the Himalayas, and the Devi came with countless eyes:\nSHATAKSHI. Every eye wept for nine nights, and her tears became rivers. She fed the world from her own hands:\nSHAKAMBHARI.\n\nThen Durgama came with a thousand armies. She shielded the gods and rishis inside a ring of light and stood outside,\nalone. Goddesses burst out of her body (Kalika, Tarini, Bhairavi, Bagala, Chhinnamasta), and in ten days his armies were\ngone. On the eleventh day she drew fifteen arrows: his horses, his charioteer, his flag, his eyes, his arms, and five\nthrough his heart. She gave the Vedas back and said: \"I killed Durgama. So my name is DURGA.\" (Devi Bhagavata Purana 7.28)\n\n📚 Meet her nine forms in our Navadurga picture books for kids: Books 1–3, set of 3 for ₹500 at rishikatha.com (link in bio)\n\nIs your name DURGA, SHATAKSHI or SHAKAMBHARI? Comment it 👇 Save this for Navratri and share it with someone named Durga!\n\n#maadurga #durga #jaimaadurga #navratri #shakambhari #shatakshi #devibhagavatam #hindumythology #indianmythology\n#sanatandharma #durgamaa #mythologystories #kidsbooks #rishikatha #hindugoddess", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1792074976, "like_count": 6995, "comment_count": 49, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-1086958987457027a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 68.262, "asr": 48000, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.fblr22-1.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQNJCLuL4giopOOYF3NbOAofmFiL3zSseEa0Gk1vdEYpzTp3ZoNCPCxK9i9UKETCYUAvUnXiKt